data type_decl_field_decl_block_not_named_at_graft: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "type_decl_field_decl_block_not_named_at_graft" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a type_decl whose parse tree still carries dag_surface_field_decl_block is not rehomed onto a Named graft edge** (INVALID STATE: namespace_graft_type_decl_named_edge returns Absent whenever parse_subtree_locate_production finds that production under the unit. The skip is that production, not the record spelling. dag_grammar_type_variant_expr puts an optional field_decl_block on every variant, and graft runs after sugar, so the same arm covers `type Rec { n: Int }`, `type Foo = Bar {}`, and `type Box = Leaf | Cell { n: Int }`. Nullary coproducts without a field block (`type Flag = On | Off`) and type_decl units that locate no field_decl_block are Named. Narrowing the skip by type_alias_rhs / `=` is not available: those discriminators rehome records.)",

    "HARM: a fielded type_decl name is not a first-class module member. Residual reconstruct keeps the unit beside a sibling Named graft so the shell is not silently deleted; that is mitigation of drop, not Named rehome. The kept shell is UNLOWERED (body_lower_type_decl rehomes only a where-clause type_decl), so its surface tokens reach resolve as bare mentions: a closure without the parse-phase declaration index refuses resolve_reason_unbound_symbol -- measured 2026-09-19 for `type Rec { }` alone and for a record beside a Named coproduct; the production route resolves the same shell through that index, which is why the corpus floor does not red. Naming the record to its captured shell instead of skipping it refuses identically (measured), so the skip is not the cause and Naming is not the climb. Record assemble refuses today. Fielded-variant assemble is in the skipped population and is not enrolled as a Named-green path.",

    "DISCRIMINATOR: RED while the skip remains `locate field_decl_block → Absent`. GREEN when body_lower_type_decl rehomes every field_decl_block type_decl onto Named containment and the skip is deleted. Nullary-coproduct Named is a different, already-green population and does not stand for this class.",

    "EVIDENCE ENROLLED: v2.test.claim.declaration_graft_assemble declaration_graft_record_type_only_does_not_accept_today and declaration_graft_record_construct_does_not_accept_today (`!assemble_accepts`) cover the record spelling of the skip; declaration_graft_coproduct_beside_record_refuses_unbound_today asserts the typed refusal (resolve_reason_unbound_symbol) of the kept shell beside a Named sibling. No enrolled witness asserts Named for a fielded variant. They flip to permanent regression controls when that spelling accepts, they do not retire.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable -- residual reconstruct contains the drop; the invalid Named-absence is still writable. CEILING: 3 once body_lower_type_decl is the Named home for field_decl_block type_decl, so graft need not skip.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: body_lower_type_decl rehomes a field_decl_block type_decl onto a Named containment edge (the capability tracked as gunbc#11582), and namespace_graft_type_decl_named_edge no longer returns Absent on that production. Nothing smaller retires this row: landing 11582 without that rehome, or deleting the skip without the lowering, is not the climb. Closing only the record spelling while fielded variants still skip is not the climb.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
